HST Office: "Multiple" line spacing in lines, as in Word.

The Paragraph dialog (Indents and Spacing) and the custom value of the Line Spacing popup (ribbon,
sidebar) showed proportional spacing as a whole percentage, minimum 6 %. A Word user who typed "1.3"
got 13 % (the dot is the thousands separator in a Vietnamese locale) and "1,3" got 6 %, without a
message, and the lines overlapped.

- The "Multiple" field shows and reads a number of lines with two decimals ("1,30"), range 0.06 to
  132 lines, steps of 0.5 lines. "1,3" and "1.3" are 130 % in any locale; a value typed with "%"
  ("130%") is a percentage. svx/source/dialog/hstlinespacing.cxx (SPDX LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary)
  parses and formats; the field's value is the percentage, so the attribute (SvxLineSpacingItem,
  DOCX w:line/240, ODF fo:line-height) is unchanged: DOCX w:line="312" opens as 1,30 and saves as 312.
- The popup gets the quick values 2.5 and 3 next to 1, 1.15, 1.5 and 2, and "Line Spacing Options..."
  which opens the Paragraph dialog on Indents and Spacing (every paragraph dialog names that page
  "indents"; the page the dialog restores is set before the dispatch).
- Writer, Calc (text in shapes), Impress and Draw share the page and the popup, so all of them get it.

License: the upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the hst* files are HST's.
Test: CppunitTest_svx_hst_line_spacing; tests/runtime/dialogs_writer_paragraph_font_cases.py
